{"timestamp": 1779428245.0699565, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I found Alice's dead body in security. I just came up from navigation. Here's exactly what I saw: around tick 4, I was in navigation and saw Frank walk in, coming from security. I then moved up to security myself, arriving at tick 6, where I found Alice dead. Eve was standing right there in security with the body when I walked in. \n\nEve, what happened? Were you just walking in too, or were you there when it happened? Frank, did you see Alice alive when you left security? I'm just putting the facts out there, let's hear from Eve and Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779428263.0490494, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Charlie's timeline matches mine perfectly. I started in weapons, went through security, and headed down to navigation. I got to navigation around tick 4 and saw Charlie leaving to head up to security. \n\nTo answer your question, Charlie: no, I did not see Alice at all when I walked through security. The room was completely empty when I was there. So the murder had to happen after I left.\n\nI also have some important info about Eve. Right at the start of the round (tick 1), I was in weapons and I saw Eve walk in, coming from security. If she was found standing next to the body in security at tick 6 like Charlie says, she must have looped back around. \n\nEve, you have some explaining to do. Let's hear your side of the story, and I want to hear from everyone else before we decide who to vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779428273.5050466, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I've been stuck in storage doing tasks this entire round and haven't seen a single soul, so I don't have any direct evidence to add about the murder itself. \n\nHowever, Charlie and Frank's stories line up perfectly regarding their movement around navigation at tick 4. If Frank is telling the truth that security was empty when he passed through, Alice must have arrived there after he left. \n\nThe biggest question mark here is obviously Eve. Charlie, you said Eve was standing right there with the body when you walked in. Eve, if you didn't kill Alice, why didn't you report the body? Did you just walk into the room at the exact same time as Charlie, or were you hesitating? We definitely need to hear your side of the story before we make any decisions. Let's hear from the rest of you."}}
{"timestamp": 1779428300.4206262, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I started in security, went up to weapons right away \u2014 Frank seeing me there at tick 1 is true. I stayed on weapons for a bit, then came back down toward security because I still had the camera/security task.\n\nWhen I got back into security, Alice was already down, and Charlie came in from navigation basically at the same moment and hit report before I could. I wasn\u2019t \u201cstanding there hesitating\u201d for ages \u2014 it was literally immediate from my perspective.\n\nFrank saying security was empty when he passed through actually fits with this: Alice must\u2019ve come in after he left. But that doesn\u2019t make it automatically me. Someone could\u2019ve come from electrical, killed, and left before Charlie came up. Did anyone see Diana this round? I haven\u2019t heard her route yet, and electrical connects right into security."}}
{"timestamp": 1779428332.7890072, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "To answer your question, Eve, I started in the cafeteria, moved down to medbay, and I had just arrived in electrical when this meeting was called. I haven't seen a single soul this entire round, so I definitely wasn't in security. Nice try trying to deflect onto me, though.\n\nLet's synthesize what we know: we only have one Duck in this game. Charlie and Frank vouch for each other's crossover in navigation, which effectively clears them both since there aren't two Ducks to fake a corroborating story. Frank confirmed security was empty when he passed through, meaning Alice had to enter security *after* Frank left. Eve, you admit you went back down to security. Charlie then walks in and finds you directly standing on the body. \n\nYour only defense is that Charlie reported it instantly before you could, but combined with your immediate attempt to cast suspicion into electrical, it looks incredibly guilty. You were caught at the scene of the crime, and the only other people in the area clear each other's timelines. Bob is isolated in storage doing tasks, and I wasn't anywhere near security. \n\nYou were caught red-handed, Eve. I am voting for Eve, and I highly suggest everyone else does the same so we can win this."}}
